id: core/lacuna
title: "lacuna"
kind: core
status: v1
updated: 2026-08-17

definition: >
  A lacuna is a typed inadequacy or discrepancy between the current state
  model and a relevant target, requirement, unanswered question, boundary, or
  proof condition. A target is optional; a lacuna is not proof that a goal
  should exist.

not_the_same_as:
  - failure
  - flaw
  - task
  - destiny
  - proof
  - desire
  - target

kinds:
  - missing_knowledge
  - missing_evidence
  - missing_permission
  - missing_resource
  - missing_skill
  - unresolved_conflict
  - unratified_target
  - unselected_choice
  - blocked_dependency
  - threatened_boundary
  - unverified_result

questions:
  - what is missing
  - what is unknown
  - what is blocked
  - what cannot yet be assumed
  - what would make the next move safer

use: >
  Name the lacuna before choosing a move. If the lacuna is unclear, the next
  move may be observation rather than action.

proof:
  source:
    - readme.yawn
    - core/movement-loop.yawn
    - core/co-orientation-loop.yawn
    - migrations/2026-08-17-canonical-extension.yawn
  status: seed-backed
